":"CRB2","gene_id":"ENSG00000148204","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.964305,"donor_log2fc":0.022266,"donor_lfcse":0.115021,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00078582,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"CRB2","gene_symbol_current":"CRB2","gene_id":"ENSG00000148204","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":8.18369e-26,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.270563,"nucleus_score":-10.6669,"pct_ad":0.154482,"pct_control":0.184894,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.963934,"donor_log2fc":-0.077462,"donor_lfcse":0.221349,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00164341,"degas_log2fc":0.122077,"degas_padj":2.61145e-05}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000148204","module":"red","kme":0.203047,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.796936,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000148204","entrez_id":["286204"],"uniprot":["Q5IJ48"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a member of a family of proteins that are components of the Crumbs cell polarity complex. In mammals, members of this family are thought to play a role in many cellular processes in early embryonic development. A similar protein in Drosophila determines apicobasal polarity in embryonic epithelial cells. Mutations in this gene are associated with focal segmental glomerulosclerosis 9, and with ventriculomegaly with cystic kidney disease. [provided by RefSeq, Aug 2016].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q5IJ48","text":"Apical polarity protein that plays a central role during the epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition (EMT) at gastrulation, when newly specified mesodermal cells move inside the embryo (By similarity). Acts by promoting cell ingression, the process by which cells leave the epithelial epiblast and move inside the embryo to form a new tissue layer (By similarity). The anisotropic distribution of CRB2 and MYH10/myosin-IIB at cell edges define which cells will ingress: cells with high apical CRB2 are probably extruded from the epiblast by neighboring cells with high levels of apical MYH10/myosin-IIB (By similarity). Plays a role in the maintenance of retinal neuroepithelium organization, structural integrity, adhesion, photoreceptor polarity and retinal photoreceptor layer thickness (By similarity). May play a role in determining the length of cone photoreceptor outer segments and proliferation of late-born progenitor cells (By similarity). Also required for maintenance of the apical polarity complex during development of the cortex (By similarity). Inhibits gamma-secretase-dependent cleavage of APP and secretion of amyloid-beta peptide 40 and amyloid-beta peptide 42, and thereby inhibits gamma-secretase-dependent Notch transcription (PubMed:20299451)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}